72.00 673.89 451.28 0.70 re f
/F2 11.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 645.89 Tm
(Abstract) Tj
/F3 9.8 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 755.29 Tm
(We present a workspace architecture in which an agent session, its file tree, and its rendered) Tj
/F3 9.8 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 742.69 Tm
(artifacts share a single surface. The design keeps a strict separation between a rendering-only) Tj
/F3 9.8 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 730.09 Tm
(frontend and a sidecar that owns all business logic, and we show that the resulting system) Tj
/F3 9.8 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 717.49 Tm
(sustains trees with hundreds of thousands of nodes without measurable frame cost.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 691.49 Tm
(1  Introduction) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 702.09 Tm
(Tool-using agents are usually constrained by the surface they can observe. A flat file) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 688.69 Tm
(list, a paginated tree, or a transcript without inline artifacts all force the model into a) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 675.29 Tm
(lossy summary of its own workspace. We argue that the file tree is the primary context) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 661.89 Tm
(surface for research work, and that a session which can address any node of that tree, at) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 648.49 Tm
(any depth, without loading it into a dialog, is materially more capable.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 629.09 Tm
(Our contribution is architectural rather than algorithmic. The renderer stores a normalized) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 615.69 Tm
(map and derives rows on demand; the sidecar owns the session and emits a newline-delimited) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 602.29 Tm
(protocol; the boundary between them is a single total function that classifies frames.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 576.29 Tm
(2  Related Work) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 586.89 Tm
(Earlier editors modelled the workspace as a widget. Linear-time tree projections, virtual) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 573.49 Tm
(scrolling, and incremental stores are all well understood individually; the novelty here is) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.00 560.09 Tm
(refusing to persist any of them in the view layer.) Tj
endstream
endobj
